Alembic migrations for QuantDesk.

  qd migrate            apply everything pending (alembic upgrade head)
  qd migrate --status   current revision vs head, applies nothing
  qd migrate --sql      print the DDL instead of running it

Writing one:

  alembic revision -m "add whatever"

There is no --autogenerate. See the reasoning in env.py: the schema is
hand-written SQL with Timescale hypertables, and autogenerate proposes
dropping the chunk tables Timescale manages. Write the SQL by hand, and
write a real downgrade() — "schema changes on a live trading DB need to be
reversible" (ARCHITECTURE.md §2) is the whole reason Alembic is here.

db/schema.sql is the 0001 baseline and is applied by Postgres on first boot
via /docker-entrypoint-initdb.d. Migrations move forward FROM it; do not
edit schema.sql to make a schema change, or a fresh install and an upgraded
one will disagree.
